  <string name="learn_samatha_title">Samatha and relaxed alertness</string>
  <string name="learn_samatha_body">Samatha in practice points toward calm collectedness. This app tries to reward relaxed alertness rather than quiet drowsiness, so the feedback signal fades down when the frontal pattern looks sleepy or contaminated.</string>
  <string name="learn_calibration_title">How calibration works</string>
  <string name="learn_calibration_body">The clean baseline calibration lasts 60 seconds. For the first 30 seconds you sit still with your eyes open; for the second 30 seconds you relax your face and close your eyes. These clean windows set your personal median and MAD baselines for the classifier.</string>
  <string name="learn_artifact_calibration_title">Optional artefact calibration</string>
  <string name="learn_artifact_calibration_body">After the clean baseline, you can run a short 25-second artefact capture. It records eye movements, jaw clench, and forehead tension so blink and EMG thresholds can be personalised without contaminating the clean meditation baseline.</string>
  <string name="learn_score_title">Frontal-state feedback proxy</string>
  <string name="learn_score_body">The live reward is a personalised frontal-state classifier built from 8-second raw EEG windows. Dashboard audio uses the source chosen in the Session card, while the games use their own fixed multi-channel EEG mappings.</string>
  <string name="learn_metric_difference_title">Settled is not drowsy</string>
  <string name="learn_metric_difference_body">Drowsiness is estimated first so the app does not confuse sleepy theta-heavy slowing with useful meditation feedback. Its evidence combines TAR, TBR, entropy, and ABR, so a settled state here means relaxed and awake, not merely low-energy.</string>
  <string name="learn_caveat_title">Interpretation limits</string>
  <string name="learn_caveat_body">This is a non-medical training aid built around one dry frontal electrode at FP1 with an ear reference. It cannot infer whole-brain state, connectivity, source localisation, or meditative attainment.</string>
  <string name="learn_wellbeing_title">Wellbeing note</string>
  <string name="learn_wellbeing_body">If you feel discomfort, fatigue, or stress during sessions, pause and recover before continuing. Quietness alone is not the goal; stable, alert practice is.</string>
